1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,750
Meet Cowork Value Intelligence.

2
00:00:02,751 --> 00:00:11,819
This data-free Power BI template connects observed Cowork activity with transparent value assumptions, customer-priced consumption, and evidence-aware recommendations.

3
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:15,122
It comes to life with your approved customer exports.

4
00:00:15,123 --> 00:00:20,468
Here is a guided tour of the decisions it supports and the boundaries that keep those decisions defensible.

5
00:00:21,233 --> 00:00:24,017
Start Here is the report's decision map.

6
00:00:24,018 --> 00:00:30,920
It routes leaders to value, cost, methodology, data connection, business-unit, and user-tier questions.

7
00:00:30,921 --> 00:00:37,673
Begin with the decision you need to make, then confirm that the page's required source files and customer inputs are available.

8
00:00:38,441 --> 00:00:47,799
The Executive Summary starts with observed active users and task volume, then adds modeled value, effective platform cost, and return under the selected assumptions.

9
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:51,544
Reconciliation and completeness indicators remain visible.

10
00:00:51,545 --> 00:00:58,586
Treat the result as scenario-based decision support, not causality, audited savings, or realized cash return.

11
00:00:59,345 --> 00:01:05,042
Task Categories and Methodology explains what people delegate and how that work becomes modeled value.

12
00:01:05,043 --> 00:01:10,774
Task volume, scheduled share, and mapping coverage are observed or derived from source records.

13
00:01:10,775 --> 00:01:15,997
Minutes saved are published assumptions applied to each category, not measured task duration.

14
00:01:16,745 --> 00:01:21,248
The Methodology and Value Calculator keeps every major assumption visible.

15
00:01:21,249 --> 00:01:30,763
Compare baseline and adjusted value, inspect category sensitivity, and record the selected labor rate, estimate basis, billing mode, and price inputs.

16
00:01:30,764 --> 00:01:36,332
The hidden assumptions page contains the underlying action catalog and research-backed minute ranges.

17
00:01:37,112 --> 00:01:43,300
Value versus Cost compares modeled value with customer-priced observed consumption under the selected billing mode.

18
00:01:43,301 --> 00:01:47,558
Read credit bands and value bands separately before using the ratio.

19
00:01:47,559 --> 00:01:54,578
Re-run the page with Finance-approved terms and test whether the conclusion survives changes in both cost and value assumptions.

20
00:01:55,328 --> 00:02:02,978
Value by Department shows how observed tasks, credits, modeled value, and allocated cost distribute across business units.

21
00:02:02,979 --> 00:02:06,388
Check identity-match coverage before comparing teams.

22
00:02:06,389 --> 00:02:15,015
Differences may reflect population, work mix, consumption, or missing organization data, so pair the page with business context before acting.

23
00:02:15,776 --> 00:02:22,612
Value by User Tier reveals whether activity and modeled value are broadly distributed or concentrated among a smaller group.

24
00:02:22,613 --> 00:02:28,086
The percentile split requires at least twenty active users and changes with the filter context.

25
00:02:28,087 --> 00:02:34,571
Use it to identify enablement patterns, champions, or dependencies, not to rate employee performance.

26
00:02:35,343 --> 00:02:41,866
Right-Sizing and Reclaim combines observed credits, allowance, activity recency, and budget segments.

27
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:46,816
Near-limit, over-limit, inactive, and low-use flags are review prompts.

28
00:02:46,817 --> 00:02:55,042
Confirm role, leave, seasonality, manager context, and contract terms before changing access, allowance, or assignment.

29
00:02:55,791 --> 00:03:02,504
Skills and Allocated Consumption uses friendly labels for known skills and readable fallbacks for technical identifiers.

30
00:03:02,505 --> 00:03:05,266
Invocations and users are observed.

31
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:11,728
Credits, cost, and classified value are directional allocations because the source does not meter them per skill.

32
00:03:11,729 --> 00:03:16,137
Use volume for enablement and allocation only as planning context.

33
00:03:16,891 --> 00:03:21,852
Model and LLM Breakdown appears only when Purview supplies model attribution.

34
00:03:21,853 --> 00:03:28,911
The page can distribute modeled value, cost, and credits by task share, but those fields are not model-specific meters.

35
00:03:28,912 --> 00:03:31,947
If model data is unavailable, stop.

36
00:03:31,948 --> 00:03:36,668
Obtain source-backed metering before recommending a model on cost or efficiency.

37
00:03:37,435 --> 00:03:40,476
The Metric Glossary is the final quality gate.

38
00:03:40,477 --> 00:03:46,788
It defines each metric, its calculation, evidence condition, source dependency, and limitation.

39
00:03:46,789 --> 00:03:56,051
When a result leaves the report, carry its definition, reporting period, filters, evidence label, selected assumptions, and owner into the decision record.

40
00:03:56,803 --> 00:04:05,480
That is Cowork Value Intelligence: one report that connects observed work with transparent assumptions, customer-priced consumption, and evidence-aware action.

41
00:04:05,481 --> 00:04:13,533
Download the template, connect your approved exports, challenge the inputs, and end each analysis with a clear owner and next validation step.

